# CYS component: WXClient -> Game.exe, the TLBB 0.85 game client (procedures, objects, data pools, packet handlers,
# Lua script interface, input/sound/network managers).
# Old project: Client/WXClient/WXClient.vcxproj (481 sources, Application, MultiByte, /MD; defines __WINDOWS__
# _FOX_CLIENT _FOX_LOGIN _FOX_SERVER GAME_CLIENT _DISABLE_TRACE__). 0.85 linked through 9 `#pragma comment(lib)` lines
# (shlwapi, winmm x2, dinput8 x2, dxguid x2, Ws2_32, Sound/fmod375/fmodvc.lib) plus solution project references
# (WXEngine, WXNetPackets, LuaPlus, CEGUIBase, CEGUIFalagard, CEGUISystem, WXRender). Here every dependency is an
# explicit CMake link (the fmod375 pragma is gone, the others name libraries linked below anyway).
#
# Render.dll and UI_CEGUI.dll are not linked: Game.exe loads them at run time with tKernel::LoadPlugin
# (Procedure/GameProcedure.cpp) and reaches them through the abstract tXxxSystem interfaces of Engine/Interface plus
# the tKernel class registry (NewNode("CRenderSystem"/"CUISystem"/"CResourceProvider")).
# LuaPlus comes from the UI agent's luaplus component (cys_luaplus = LuaPlus.dll, PUBLIC LUAPLUS_HAS_WCHAR_T, which
# must match between the DLL and Game.exe). CEGUI is not used by Game.exe.
# Sound: CYS_HAVE_FMOD=1 when the FMOD Core SDK is configured (imported target cys_fmod, CYSCommon.cmake) ->
# Sound/GMSound*.cpp use FMOD Core 2.02 and fmod.dll is copied next to Game.exe; otherwise sound is a silent stub.

